From 04d3c59674d2dcebea79b4091d41dc84ff20562c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:30:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): comments record origin_gateway; wait-comment
 probe; refuse author-matching wake checks; wake_probe_stale [daveey]

A parked card's wake check counted comments WHERE author='macbook'; the Mac's reply arrived through the
hermes-hub relay as 'hub:gw:macbook', so t_01a17f81686694ec stayed parked 38 h after the answer
(self-heal desktop-00c4a3bda2).

- task_comments.origin_gateway (nullable, machine-local, back-filled from hub:gw:<x> / <x>/t_... authors);
  add_comment(origin_gateway=) / 'kanban comment --origin-gateway' (relay sender), default from the author
  spelling, else this gateway.
- 'hermes kanban wait-comment <task> --after-id N [--from-gateway X] [--contains T]': 0 match, 1 not yet,
  2 cannot tell; a gateway matches origin_gateway or any author spelling of it.
- Park guard (kanban_awaiting.resolve): a wake_check filtering task_comments by author (=, like, glob, in)
  is refused with code author_probe naming the wait-comment command; author != own still parks.
  Off switch: kanban.author_probe_guard: false. wake_check tool description says so.
- Detection: wake_probe_stale. A parked card whose reason/probe names a hermes-hub request whose owner card
  is done, while its probe still exits 1, wakes once with a dispatcher comment.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_comment_origin.py (16 red before, 19 green after).
---
